<chapter xml:id="ch01_intro_robotic_subsystems_control_loop" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Introduction to Robotic Subsystems &amp; Control Loop</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>This chapter introduces the core subsystems that appear in most robotic systems, including sensing, computation, actuation, and power. You will learn how these parts interact to turn high-level goals into physical behavior. The chapter also presents the control loop as the central organizing idea behind robotic autonomy. By the end, you should be able to describe how information and commands flow through a robot during operation.</p>
  </introduction>
